   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the commissioner of the department of civil service to\nreinstate Edward P. Ackley on the eligible civil service list for employment\nas a full-time police officer for the village of Hudson Falls",
    "basePrintNo": "S9011",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9011-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S9011\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the commissioner of the department\nof civil service to reinstate Edward P.  Ackley on the eligible civil\nservice list for employment as a full-time police officer for the\nvillage of Hudson Falls\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes Edward P. Ackley to take the competitive exam for police\nofficer and be placed on the eligible list for such position in the\nVillage of Hudson Falls.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Edward P. Ackley to sit for the civil service exam\nand be placed on the eligibility list for full time police officer for\nthe Village of Hudson Falls.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date as immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDue to the provisions under the Civil Service Law, the Village of Hudson\nFalls has requested legislation to permit one of their part-time offi-\ncers, Edward P. Ackley, to be eligible to take the civil service exam-\nination since he is currently older than 35 years old.\n\nRecruiting and retaining well-qualified full time police officers is\nchallenging for small and rural police departments. At the request of\nthe Mayor of the Village of Hudson Falls and the Chief of Police, and by\nresolution of the Village Council, this bill would address this issue by\nallowing a part time police officer of the Village of Hudson Falls\nPolice Department to be eligible for full time status. While age\nrestrictions certainly have practical value, they do not always reflect\nthe ability of some candidates to perform full time police duties.\nAccording to the Chief of Police, Officer Ackley (part time since 2016)\nis perfectly competent to perform the duties required of a full time\npolice officer, rating his skills as \"exemplary\" even outperforming some\nof his younger coworkers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
